    RETURNING id INTO v_id;
  ELSE
    UPDATE public.calculators SET description = $q$Milling a slot out with an end mill, as the Machining calculator workbook's Slot Milling sheet times it: n = 1000 v / (pi D), capped at the machine's spindle limit; depth passes = slot depth / depth of cut and width passes = slot width / D, each rounded up; time = (slot length + 10 mm + D) / (feed per tooth x teeth x n) x depth passes x width passes, rounded up to whole seconds a slot. The depth of cut is the slotting depth ratio of the cutter, half its diameter (the sheet's example cuts 6.5 mm a pass with a 12 mm cutter). Cutting speed and feed per tooth from the workbook's milling conditions for the material; the cutter is the slot's width, or the material's end mill (tblMillingFinishing) when the slot is wider; the end mill's price and life from the workbook. The engine also times the slot by Plunge Milling and keeps the quicker. (It replaces the slot's volume at the material removal rate plus 20 s a slot.)$q$, updated_at = now() WHERE id = v_id;
  END IF;

